{"id":"cash-nonprofits-grants-to-individuals","title":"Funded nonprofits that report grants to individuals","question":"Which City-funded nonprofits tell the tax authority they gave money or cash-like help to individuals, and how large is that beside what the City paid them?","finding":"96 organizations paid $100,000 or more by the City in the year of their latest return report grants or assistance to individuals in that return, $571.5 million between them; most of that is food, child-care subsidies and rent paid on people’s behalf. 30 of them label $25,000 or more of it as stipends, cash, gift cards, incentives or financial assistance: $25.9 million in all, led by Catholic Charities ($16.9 million); Compass Family Services ($1.8 million); PRC ($1.3 million); Jewish Voc & Career Counseling Svc (Jvs) ($1.2 million). The returns do not say which funder’s money paid for these lines.","how":"Schedule I, Part III of each organization’s latest Form 990 (grants and other assistance to individuals), the latest version where a return was amended. “Labelled cash-like” adds the lines whose own label speaks of stipends, cash, gift cards, incentives, honoraria, guaranteed income, financial assistance or emergency relief, leaving out lines that also say child care, tuition, scholarship, rent, housing, utilities or food. City money is what the payment file shows for the City fiscal year in which the return’s year ended. Sorted by the cash-like figure. Recipients are the organization’s own count; nobody is named.","limits":"The label is the organization’s own and one word can cover very different things; a line called “financial assistance” may be paid to a landlord or a utility, not to the person. The return covers all of an organization’s funders, so the cash-like figure can exceed the City’s payments without any City money being involved. What would settle it: for a City-funded programme, the grantee’s ledger of stipends or cards issued against the participant roster. The payment file labels each line with a fiscal year that is not always the year the payment was issued: some earlier payments, mostly on purchase orders in multi-year capital funds, are filed under a later year, and the Controller's own published figures follow that label. Payments are dated here by voucher number, a single running sequence, which moves $5.52 billion of $119.3 billion (4.6%) to an earlier year than its label; $1.08 billion of that belongs to fiscal 2018 or earlier, before the file starts. Near the turn of a year the number dates a payment to within a few days.","tier":"REDFLAG","columns":[{"k":"org","t":"Organization","type":"org"},{"k":"yearEnd","t":"Return for year ended","type":"date"},{"k":"toIndividuals","t":"Grants and assistance to individuals","type":"usd"},{"k":"cashLike","t":"Of which labelled cash-like","type":"usd"},{"k":"labels","t":"Its labels","type":"text"},{"k":"recipients","t":"Recipients it reports","type":"int"},{"k":"cityPaid","t":"City paid it that year","type":"usd"},{"k":"cashAgainstCity","t":"Cash-like against City money","type":"pct"},{"k":"allYears","t":"To individuals, all returns on file","type":"usd"}],"rows":[{"org":"Catholic Charities","orgKey":"CATHOLIC CHARITIES","yearEnd":"2025-06-30","toIndividuals":16895009,"cashLike":16895009,"labels":"Financial assistance","recipients":55648,"cityPaid":32576687,"cashAgainstCity":0.5186,"allYears":65252961},{"org":"Compass Family Services","orgKey":"COMPASS FAMILY SERVICES","yearEnd":"2025-06-30","toIndividuals":19951527,"cashLike":1761208,"labels":"Client assistance - miscellaneous cash aids","recipients":3700,"cityPaid":29401652,"cashAgainstCity":0.0599,"allYears":41829103},{"org":"PRC","orgKey":"PRC","yearEnd":"2025-06-30","toIndividuals":1313832,"cashLike":1261957,"labels":"Emergency financial assistance","recipients":1505,"cityPaid":7901792,"cashAgainstCity":0.1597,"allYears":6240537},{"org":"Jewish Voc & Career Counseling Svc (Jvs)","orgKey":"JEWISH VOC CAREER COUNSELING SVC JVS","